# Ntfy secrets (services VM)
# Copy to .sops.env, fill, then `sops -e -i .sops.env` — encrypting a NEW
# file needs only the pubkey in .sops.yaml (no age key, no sudo);
# editing later goes through `sopsedit` (see CLAUDE.md).
#
# Ntfy reads every config key from an NTFY_<KEY> environment variable, so these
# names are load-bearing — they are not referenced from server.yml.
#
# Optional: leave the SMTP VALUES EMPTY to use phone push only (keys must
# stay — the stack-env-drift lint enforces exact key parity with this file).
# Failure alerts still work; they just do not also land in an inbox.

# Proton Mail SMTP submission for alerts@idanreed.com.
# See ServerNotes/designs/external-email.md.
NTFY_SMTP_SENDER_ADDR=smtp.protonmail.ch:587
NTFY_SMTP_SENDER_USER=alerts@idanreed.com
NTFY_SMTP_SENDER_PASS=changeme_proton_smtp_token
